===Proper noun===
{{en-prop}}

# The desire for [[wealth]] personified as an [[evil]] [[spirit]] or a [[malign#Adjective|malign]] [[influence#Noun|influence]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Matthew|6|24|passage=No man can ſerue two maſters: for either he will hate the one and loue the other, or elſe hee will holde to the one, and deſpiſe the other. Ye cannot ſerue God and '''Mammon'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=The Present Panic|magazine=[[w:Tait's Magazine|Tait's Edinburgh Magazine]]|location=Edinburgh|publisher=[[w:William Tait (publisher)|William Tait]]|month=November|year=1857|volume=XXIV|page=644|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=0QEbAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA644|oclc=1607056|passage=They [bankers] would do what has been done by the [[w:Banque de France|Bank of France]]—buy bullion at a premium, on the approach of danger, and keep peril at a safe and respectable distance. Any expenditure that might be incurred for that purpose would be small indeed when contrasted with the immense loss and suffering caused by the present system, and the continual fear in which the public now live of some new crisis—because it has been out of one and into another for a long period now; and that will be the case hereafter, until we have no interval to gather strength, and recruit for the next struggle with '''Mammon''', or [[Moloch#Proper noun 2|Moloch]], or whatever other name of evil import belongs to the "[[tutelarity|Tutelarity]]" of [[w:Lombard Street, London|Lombard-street]] and its precincts.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=306|passage=Lives sacrificed upon the altar of '''Mammon''', only units in the thousands who have fallen in the wilds of Australia, victims to the fever and unrest caused by the search for gold.}}
# ''Often'' '''{{l|en|mammon}}''': [[wealth]], [[material]] [[avarice]], [[profit]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Edwin Mullins|Edwin [B.] Mullins]]|title=The Popes of Avignon: A Century in Exile|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=BlueBridge|year=2008|isbn=978-1-933346-15-1|page=43|passage=The proper sphere of the church, after all, was the kingdom of God, not greedy earthbound kingdoms of '''mammon''', which should be left to temporal authorities to rule and squabble over.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Michael McNay|title=Andrew Wyeth: Realist painter whose work was much loved by the US public but divided the critics [obituary]|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/artanddesign/2009/jan/19/andrew-wyeth-obituary|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160316012029/http://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2009/jan/19/andrew-wyeth-obituary|archivedate=16 March 2016|newspaper={{w|The Guardian}}|location=London|date=19 January 2009|passage=But he &#91;{{w|Andrew Wyeth}}&#93; did not want to become an all-American illustrator like the Post's illustrious Norman Rockwell&nbsp;– and he had heard his own father, an illustrator, bemoan choosing the path of '''mammon''' rather than the path of virtue, and declined.}}

